Date: Sun, 12 Jun 1994 11:20:07 -0100
Subject: [#94-6-33] Digital Cash & Free Banking

Offshore banks conected to ATM networks?  Easily done!  All the pieces are
here, at least.

Piece one: You can get a Visa card issued by a European bank, that will let
you get cash advances at ordinary American ATM machines.

Piece two: Lots of big European banks have branches in the Cayman Islands,
so you could put your account there and have it protected by the fierce
Caymanian bank secrecy laws.  Or you could use a Swiss bank, which is
protected by less fierce but still IRS-proof laws.

Piece three: With some banks, if you keep an account with them, and use a
Visa issued by them, they can set it up so that your Visa bill is
automatically paid from your savings account.

I'm not sure if any one bank offers all three of these services, but if
they haven't, it's only a matter of time.  If some bank does, you can get a
secure bank account with almost the convenience of a local account.

One problem with this method is that it doesn't permit quick and easy
deposits.  You would have to stick the check in an envelope and mail it to
the Cayman Islands.  But if we had an on-line bank that problem would go
away.


